  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) to Address the Most Urgent Needs of the Drought Affected Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Kenya, an estimated 6.4 million people needed humanitarian assistance in the beginning of 2023, including over 5.4 million projected to be severely food insecure, and over 677,900 children and almost 139,000 pregnant and breastfeeding women in need of treatment for acute malnutrition in 2023. According to the International Organization for Migration (IOM)&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix, an estimated over 460,000 individuals were internally displaced in 2022-2022 across arid and semi-arid land counties. 
 
In response to the humanitarian crisis due to drought, IOM in partnership with five implementing partners (Arid Lands Development Focus, Rural Agency for Community Development and Assistance, Sustainable Approaches for Community Empowerment, Strategies for Northern Development, and Wajir South Development Association) is providing multi-purpose cash assistance to over 20,000 individuals to improve the deteriorating living conditions of target households in Marsabit, Turkana, Wajir, and Mandera counties, prioritizing the most vulnerable population. Multi-purpose cash assistance will complement the households&#x2019; purchasing power and enhance the functionality of the local economy towards stabilization and economic recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
